IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, sections 102 and 103 -- MANAGEMENT BY THE
-- DIRECTORS: the duty to manage, the number of directors, and by-laws made by the directors. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A cross-reference to
-- another module is a plain input and says so ("out of range: section N (piece X)"). The keel's input names
-- are used for the corporation being a distributing corporation and for a unanimous shareholder agreement.

§ `s 102 Duty to manage or supervise management; number of directors`

§§ `s 102(1) Duty to manage or supervise management`

-- "Subject to any unanimous shareholder agreement": the duty yields to the extent an agreement transfers the
-- matter away from the directors (out of range: section 146 (piece cb3)).
-- src:1201 | Duty to manage or supervise management
-- src:1202 | 102 (1) Subject to any unanimous shareholder agreement, the directors shall manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of a corporation.
@ref CBCA s 102(1) (src:1201-1202)
GIVEN `there is a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement restricts the powers of the directors in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors must manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs within s 102(1)` MEANS
    NOT (    `there is a unanimous shareholder agreement`
         AND `the agreement restricts the powers of the directors in the matter`)

§§ `s 102(2) Number of directors`

-- src:1203 | Number of directors
-- src:1204 | (2) A corporation shall have one or more directors but a distributing corporation, any of the issued securities of which remain outstanding and are held by more than one person, shall have not fewer than three directors, at least two of whom are not officers or employees of the corporation or its affiliates.
@ref CBCA s 102(2) (src:1203-1204)
GIVEN `the number of directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of the issued securities of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors who are not officers or employees of the corporation or its affiliates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the number of directors complies within s 102(2)` MEANS
        `the number of directors` AT LEAST 1
    AND (    (    `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
              AND `any of the issued securities of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person`)
         IMPLIES (    `the number of directors` AT LEAST 3
                  AND `the number of directors who are not officers or employees of the corporation or its affiliates` AT LEAST 2))

§ `s 103 By-laws`

§§ `s 103(1) By-laws`

-- src:1205 | By-laws
-- src:1206 | 103 (1) Unless the articles, by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide, the directors may, by resolution, make, amend or repeal any by-laws that regulate the business or affairs of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 103(1) (src:1205-1206)
GIVEN `the by-law regulates the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may make, amend or repeal the by-law by resolution within s 103(1)` MEANS
        `the by-law regulates the business or affairs of the corporation`
    AND (NOT `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement otherwise provide`)

§§ `s 103(2) Shareholder approval`

-- src:1207 | Shareholder approval
-- src:1208 | (2) The directors shall submit a by-law, or an amendment or a repeal of a by-law, made under subsection (1) to the shareholders at the next meeting of shareholders, and the shareholders may, by ordinary resolution, confirm, reject or amend the by-law, amendment or repeal.
@ref CBCA s 103(2) (src:1207-1208)
GIVEN `the directors made, amended or repealed a by-law under subsection 103(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors must submit the by-law to the shareholders at the next meeting within s 103(2)` MEANS
    `the directors made, amended or repealed a by-law under subsection 103(1)`

-- The shareholders "may, by ordinary resolution, confirm, reject or amend": the answer is what the ordinary
-- resolution did. The input `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` is the keel's name for a passed one.
-- src:1207 | Shareholder approval
-- src:1208 | (2) The directors shall submit a by-law, or an amendment or a repeal of a by-law, made under subsection (1) to the shareholders at the next meeting of shareholders, and the shareholders may, by ordinary resolution, confirm, reject or amend the by-law, amendment or repeal.
@ref CBCA s 103(2) (src:1207-1208)
GIVEN `the by-law was submitted to the shareholders under subsection 103(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders may confirm, reject or amend the by-law within s 103(2)` MEANS
        `the by-law was submitted to the shareholders under subsection 103(2)`
    AND `the resolution is an ordinary resolution`

§§ `s 103(3) Effective date`

-- src:1209 | Effective date
-- src:1210 | (3) A by-law, or an amendment or a repeal of a by-law, is effective from the date of the resolution of the directors under subsection (1) until it is confirmed, confirmed as amended or rejected by the shareholders under subsection (2) or until it ceases to be effective under subsection (4) and, where the by-law is confirmed or confirmed as amended, it continues in effect in the form in which it was so confirmed.
@ref CBCA s 103(3) (src:1209-1210)
DECLARE `Status of a by-law made by the directors` IS ONE OF
    `in effect from the date of the directors' resolution, awaiting the shareholders`
    `in effect in the form in which the shareholders confirmed it`
    `in effect in the form in which the shareholders confirmed it as amended`
    `no longer effective`

DECLARE `What the shareholders did with a by-law` IS ONE OF
    `the shareholders confirmed it`
    `the shareholders confirmed it as amended`
    `the shareholders rejected it`
    `the shareholders have not yet acted on it`

-- Subsection (4): rejected by the shareholders, or not submitted to them as (2) requires, and the by-law
-- "ceases to be effective". "Not submitted as required" is read as: the next meeting of shareholders has been
-- held and the by-law was not submitted at it (fork F-P10-1).
-- src:1209 | Effective date
-- src:1210 | (3) A by-law, or an amendment or a repeal of a by-law, is effective from the date of the resolution of the directors under subsection (1) until it is confirmed, confirmed as amended or rejected by the shareholders under subsection (2) or until it ceases to be effective under subsection (4) and, where the by-law is confirmed or confirmed as amended, it continues in effect in the form in which it was so confirmed.
-- src:1211 | Idem
-- src:1212 | (4) If a by-law, an amendment or a repeal is rejected by the shareholders, or if the directors do not submit a by-law, an amendment or a repeal to the shareholders as required under subsection (2), the by-law, amendment or repeal ceases to be effective and no subsequent resolution of the directors to make, amend or repeal a by-law having substantially the same purpose or effect is effective until it is confirmed or confirmed as amended by the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 103(3) (src:1209-1212)
GIVEN `what the shareholders did` IS A `What the shareholders did with a by-law`
      `the next meeting of shareholders has been held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors submitted the by-law at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Status of a by-law made by the directors`
`the status of the by-law within s 103(3)` MEANS
    IF     (`what the shareholders did` EQUALS `the shareholders rejected it`)
        OR (    `the next meeting of shareholders has been held`
            AND (NOT `the directors submitted the by-law at that meeting`)
            AND (`what the shareholders did` EQUALS `the shareholders have not yet acted on it`))
    THEN `no longer effective`
    ELSE IF `what the shareholders did` EQUALS `the shareholders confirmed it`
         THEN `in effect in the form in which the shareholders confirmed it`
         ELSE IF `what the shareholders did` EQUALS `the shareholders confirmed it as amended`
              THEN `in effect in the form in which the shareholders confirmed it as amended`
              ELSE `in effect from the date of the directors' resolution, awaiting the shareholders`

§§ `s 103(4) Idem`

-- A later resolution of the directors to make, amend or repeal a by-law having substantially the same purpose
-- or effect is not effective until the shareholders confirm it, or confirm it as amended, if the earlier
-- by-law ceased to be effective under (4).
-- src:1211 | Idem
-- src:1212 | (4) If a by-law, an amendment or a repeal is rejected by the shareholders, or if the directors do not submit a by-law, an amendment or a repeal to the shareholders as required under subsection (2), the by-law, amendment or repeal ceases to be effective and no subsequent resolution of the directors to make, amend or repeal a by-law having substantially the same purpose or effect is effective until it is confirmed or confirmed as amended by the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 103(4) (src:1211-1212)
GIVEN `the earlier by-law, amendment or repeal ceased to be effective under subsection 103(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later resolution has substantially the same purpose or effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders have confirmed the later resolution or confirmed it as amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the later resolution of the directors is effective within s 103(4)` MEANS
        (NOT (    `the earlier by-law, amendment or repeal ceased to be effective under subsection 103(4)`
              AND `the later resolution has substantially the same purpose or effect`))
    OR  `the shareholders have confirmed the later resolution or confirmed it as amended`

§§ `s 103(5) Shareholder proposal`

-- "In accordance with section 137": out of range: section 137 (piece cb3).
-- src:1213 | Shareholder proposal
-- src:1214 | (5) A shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders may, in accordance with section 137, make a proposal to make, amend or repeal a by-law.
@ref CBCA s 103(5) (src:1213-1214)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder may make a proposal to make, amend or repeal a by-law within s 103(5)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder entitled to vote at an annual meeting of shareholders`
    AND `the proposal is made in accordance with section 137`
